{"book":24,"chapter":1,"context":{"chapter":1,"title":"Known Before Birth","summary":"Jeremiah, a priest's son from Anathoth, is called as a prophet to the nations while still young. God touches his mouth, shows him an almond branch and a boiling pot tilted from the north, and promises to make him a fortified city against all who oppose him.","background":"The call came in King Josiah's thirteenth year, about 627 BC, and Jeremiah's ministry ran past Jerusalem's fall in 586 BC, some forty years. Anathoth was a priestly village a few miles northeast of Jerusalem; Solomon had banished the priest Abiathar there (1 Kings 2:26), and Jeremiah may have descended from that family.","customs":[{"term":"The rod of an almond tree","verses":"1:11-12","note":"A Hebrew wordplay: 'almond' is shaqed and 'watching' is shoqed. The almond blossoms first in late winter, as if awake early; God is 'watching' over His word (KJV 'hasten')."}],"watchFor":["Six verbs in v. 10: four to tear down, two to build up.","'I cannot speak: for I am a child' (v. 6) echoes Moses' excuse.","'I am with thee… to deliver thee' frames the call (vv. 8, 19)."],"connections":["Exodus 4:10-12","1 Kings 2:26","Galatians 1:15","Isaiah 6:7"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["דִּבְרֵי","divrei","H1697","HNcmpc","[the] words of"],["יִרְמְיָהוּ","yirmeyahu","H3414","HNpm","Jeremiah"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["חִלְקִיָּהוּ","chilkiyahu","H2518","HNpm","Hilkiah"],["מִן","min-","H4480","HR","one of"],["הַכֹּהֲנִים","hakohanim","H3548","HTd/Ncmpa","the priests"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","who"],["בַּעֲנָתוֹת","ba'anatot","H6068","HR/Npl","[were] at Anathoth"],["בְּאֶרֶץ","be'eretz","H776","HR/Ncfsc","in [the] land of"],["בִּנְיָמִן","binyamin","H1144","HNpm","Benjamin"]],"x":[[13006060,13006060,3],[14036021,14036021,3],[24011021,24011021,3],[24032007,24032009,3],[26001003,26001003,3]],"xn":5},"2":{"w":[["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","whom"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["דְבַר","devar-